{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression intercept linear regression intercept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Intercept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Intercept","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Regression Analysis]] · [[Linear Model Design and Contrasts]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression intercept linear regression intercept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Intercept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Intercept","heading":"Linear Regression Intercept","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The linear regression intercept is the model's predicted outcome when every numeric predictor equals zero and every indicator is in its reference state. It anchors the fitted equation from which other coefficients add or subtract.\n\nThe intercept may lack a practical interpretation when zero is outside the observed range or the combined reference profile is unrealistic. Centering predictors can give it a more meaningful reference without changing the fitted relationships.\n\nFor a two-group indicator design in the source, the intercept equals the fitted mean of the reference group. The indicator coefficient then adds the estimated difference needed to reach the second group mean.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression intercept linear regression intercept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Intercept.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Intercept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Intercept","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}